A||||2||David DeVoe|| 2.8  oil pressure sending unit and pipe||||1||
Z||000000||David DeVoe||12-08-2001||08:38 AM||||How do you get the sending unit off the pipe its mounted on. When I tried to remove the pipe from the filter boss it broke. I've had no luck getting the sending unit off. BTW does anyone make a replacement pipe or is that strictly junkyard stuff?<BR>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||12-08-2001||07:49 PM||||To remove the sending unit, I hold the block it screws into with an open end wrench (9/16"? I don't remember for sure, sorry), and unscrew the sender with another wrench (don't remember size) on the hex underneath.<P>I am supposing you already tried something like this, and still can't get the sender to unscrew from the block.  If so, I guess all I can recommend is to use Liquid Wrench on the threads.<P>To get the tube off the engine block, I had success using a "line wrench" - basically a box end with a slot cut in it so it'll slip over the tube.  Removing oil filter will help the access.  If it's stubborn, Liquid Wrench would be a good idea.<P>Don't know if anyone makes replacement tubes, but you might try contacting some of the "Fiero Parts Vendors" (see link at bottom of this page).  If that doesn't work, you might have to have one made, using the  pieces of the old tube as a pattern.  I'm pretty sure there are people in my town who could do it if I needed one.   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||oneof547||12-08-2001||11:13 PM||||Howdy,<P>Here is a URL that will make the uninstall/<BR>install as driving your FIERO fast. Thank-Goodeness for all of us FIERO owners & for PENNOCKS!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012763.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012763.html</A> <P>Laters,<P>oneof547<BR>1988 Formula T-Tops<p>[This message has been edited by oneof547 (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||1
